The  driver  supports the following adapters: The driver provides
support for USB adapters based on the ASIX  Electronics  AX88172,
AX88178,  AX88772, AX88772A, AX88772B USB 2.0 chipsets.  The chip
contains a 10/100 MAC with MII interface and is designed to  work
with both and HomePNA transceivers.  The AX88172 and AX88772 con‐
tain  10/100 Ethernet MACs with MII interfaces.  The AX88178 con‐
tains a 10/100/1000 Gigabit MAC with a GMII/MII  interface.   The
chip  also  supports USB 2.0, thereby accommodating 100 Mb/s data
rates.  The driver supports the following media types: Enable au‐
tomatic selection of the media type and options.  Set 10Mbps  op‐
eration.   The  option can also be used to enable operation.  Not
specifying implies mode.  Set 100Mbps (fast operation.   The  op‐
tion  can  also  be used to enable operation.  Not specifying im‐
plies mode.  Set 1000Mbps (Gigabit operation (AX88178 only).  The
driver supports the following media options:  Force  full  duplex
operation.   The  interface  will  operate in half duplex mode if
this media option is not specified.  For more information on con‐
figuring this device, see See for diagnostics.  The device driver
first appeared in and was ported to It replaces the uax driver.
